    <marc:datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
      <marc:subfield code="a">Looks at the aftermath of the tragic events of 12 October 2002, from the Balinese point of view.  Two bombs exploded in Kuta.  John Darling, an Australian filmmaker who had lived in Bali for some 17 years, felt instense pain for everyone touch by the tragedy.  The healing of Bali lets those affected by the blasts tell their own personal, inmate stories.  Filemed over nine-month period, the program reveals the grieving and gradual recovery of each of those interviewed.</marc:subfield>
